	<PersonSchema slot="head" profilePage />
	<div data-ui-language-panel="en" lang="en">
		<p>
			สวัสดีครับ — I'm <strong>Vorrapong Kertnat</strong>, everyone calls me <strong class="alias">ICE</strong>
		</p>

		<p>
			I'm a full-stack developer at the <strong
				>Bank for Agriculture and Agricultural Cooperatives (BAAC)</strong
			> in Bangkok. I studied Computer Engineering at Prince of Songkla University, graduated in 2021,
			and have been building software professionally ever since — mostly TypeScript, mostly on systems
			that real people depend on.
		</p>

		<h2>What I'm into right now</h2>

		<p>
			In June 2026 I started a master's in <strong>Financial Engineering</strong> at the UTCC Graduate
			School, and it has quietly taken over my side projects. My GitHub has drifted away from web APIs
			and toward portfolio analytics, risk models, and QuantLib experiments. It turns out that after a
			few years of building banking systems, I wanted to understand the math running underneath them.
		</p>

		<p>
			By day I'm at BAAC, working mostly in Vue and ElysiaJS. By night it's coursework, portfolio math, and the occasional video game.
		</p>

		<h2>What I build with</h2>

		<p>
			TypeScript is my daily driver. On the backend I reach for <strong>ElysiaJS</strong> — I like it
			enough that I've contributed to its documentation — along with NestJS and Express. On the front
			end, React and Vue. For data: PostgreSQL, MongoDB, SQL Server, and Oracle.
		</p>

		<p>
			A good chunk of my job is DevSecOps, so I spend a lot of time with Docker, Kubernetes,
			OpenShift, ArgoCD, Helm, Jenkins, SonarQube, Trivy, and Ansible. On the side I've been learning
			<strong>Rust </strong> — slowly, and stubbornly.
		</p>

